# Cloudflare Pages edge response headers.
# Applied to every response. Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE IS THE FALLBACK, NOT WHAT PRODUCTION SERVES.
# `npm run build` copies /public into /dist and then runs
# scripts/generate-robots.ts, which OVERWRITES dist/_headers with a version it
# builds in code. Whatever is written here is replaced before deploy. Any change
# made here has to be mirrored into the `headers.push(...)` sequence in
# scripts/generate-robots.ts or it will never reach a visitor — including the
# hashed-asset fix below, which is currently mirrored NOWHERE.
#
# Security baseline added 2026-06-26 to fix missing HSTS / X-Frame-Options /
# CSP / nosniff flagged by SEO audit (60 critical security findings).
#
# NOTE on CSP: the site loads GTM, GA, Meta Pixel, Yandex Metrika and inline
# bootstrap scripts. The allowlist below is enforced and limited to the exact
# observed services. Metrika contributes one host — mc.yandex.ru — to
# script-src, connect-src and frame-src; the noscript pixel is covered by the
# existing `img-src https:`.
#
# connect-src carries that host twice, under both schemes. Webvisor is on for
# counter 111312750 and it uploads over `wss://mc.yandex.ru/solid.ws`; a CSP
# source expression matches by scheme, so `https://mc.yandex.ru` alone does not
# authorise the socket. Production consoles were logging "Connecting to
# 'wss://mc.yandex.ru/solid.ws' violates the following Content Security Policy
# directive" on every page, so the recordings the ym-hide-content masking was
# written for were never actually being made. Still one host, still no wildcard.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://connect.facebook.net https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://mc.yandex.ru; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data:; img-src 'self' data: https: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://www.google-analytics.com https://region1.google-analytics.com https://analytics.google.com https://region1.analytics.google.com https://stats.g.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://connect.facebook.net https://www.facebook.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://mc.yandex.ru wss://mc.yandex.ru https://ov-1d104299d2a447049cdc73700c9309f7.ecs.us-west-2.on.aws https://*.run.app https://*.ecs.us-east-1.on.aws; frame-src 'self' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://td.doubleclick.net https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://www.facebook.com https://mc.yandex.ru; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://www.facebook.com; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# The `/*` Cache-Control above is the HTML policy and it stays scoped to HTML:
# browsers always revalidate (max-age=0) and only the Cloudflare edge holds a
# copy, for an hour, with a day of stale-while-revalidate. It is deliberately
# NOT lengthened here — a prerendered page must be replaceable within the hour
# after a content deploy, and no rule below re-applies it to a document.
#
# What follows fixes the other half. `_headers` MERGES every matching block
# instead of letting the most specific one win, so a hashed asset was answered
# with the HTML policy and the asset policy joined together:
#
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400,
#                  public, max-age=31536000, immutable
#
# A parser takes the first directive of each kind, so the browser saw
# max-age=0 and the edge saw s-maxage=3600: a file whose URL changes whenever
# its bytes change was revalidated on every navigation and evicted from the
# edge after an hour. That is the whole point of content hashing, undone.
#
# `! Cache-Control` detaches a header applied by a more pervasive rule
# (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/ — "Detach a
# header"). The detach and the new value are written as two blocks, in that
# order, so the sequence is unambiguous: drop the inherited HTML policy, then
# state the asset policy on its own. Both paths below contain build output only
# — Vite's hashed bundles and the admin panel's hashed chunks. No document is
# served from either, so no HTML gains a long edge TTL from this.

# Bormi Admin (owner control center): the shell's headers are NOT here.
# `_headers` merges matching blocks instead of letting the specific one win, so
# a /admin/* block would be appended to the global one above and produce a
# self-contradicting Cache-Control and a malformed X-Frame-Options.
# functions/admin/[[path]].ts serves the shell and sets its own headers.
#
# What stays here is the one path that Function does not handle: the panel's
# hashed chunks, excluded in _routes.json and served from the asset store.
/admin/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control

/admin/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet

# Long-cache immutable build assets (hashed filenames).
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
